    "created_at": "2021-03-17T10:55:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-17T10:55:51Z",
    "body": "The `~/.config/gcloud/` directory contains valuable project settings that you might want to reuse when re-logging to `gcloud`.\r\n\r\nAnother way of disabling the starship gcp module would be by deleting the `~/.config/gcloud/active_config` file, but that file gets recreated as soon as you do something with `gcloud`, even without logging in. `gcloud` doesn't let you deactivate the `default` profile from the CLI, at least one configuration must be active even when logged out.\r\n\r\nAs a starship user I only care about any GCP info when I'm logged in. Would it make sense to only activate the starship GCloud module only when logged in? The change seems pretty straightforward, I can send the PR myself if that's alright with you, @mickimnet.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
